From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: msm8994: keep the root port awake while the RC is reinitialised

The second bring-up pass tears the root complex down (clocks and PHY off)
while the root port is still registered. If the PM core runtime-suspends the
root port in that window, pci_pm_runtime_suspend() -> pci_save_state() reads
its config space, which on an unclocked DWC core is a synchronous external
abort: the kworker dies with irqs disabled and the phone freezes.

Forbid runtime PM on the root port before the teardown.

---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1006,6 +1006,17 @@ static void qcom_pcie_host_post_msm8994(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 	if (!dw_pcie_link_up(pci)) {
 		dev_info(pci->dev, "first pass trained no link, redoing it powered\n");
 
+		{
+			/* runtime suspend would read config space with the RC off */
+			struct pci_dev *rp = pci_get_slot(pp->bridge->bus,
+							  PCI_DEVFN(0, 0));
+
+			if (rp) {
+				pm_runtime_forbid(&rp->dev);
+				pci_dev_put(rp);
+			}
+		}
+
 		QTRACE(pci->dev, "P1 host_deinit start");
 		qcom_pcie_host_deinit(pp);
 		QTRACE(pci->dev, "P2 host_deinit done");
